Give PredefinedPortGroupsIds a fixed underlying type.

The enumerators are written as (uint32_t)-1 .. -3 and are compared against
uint32_t group ids. With the Itanium ABI the implementation picks unsigned
int as the underlying type and that works, but under the Microsoft ABI an
unscoped enum without a fixed type is int, so the values wrap to -1 .. -3
and every "switch (uint32_t groupId) { case kPortGroupNone: }" is rejected:
"case value evaluates to -1, which cannot be narrowed to type uint32_t".

Spelling the underlying type makes the intended values ABI-independent.

